From 25002b41e343d1a3b6850959b8de22e912552430 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lineage-build <build@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:57:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cancunf: Make libcamhal_pad global

With libcamhal_pad loaded as the first DT_NEEDED of camerahalserver
(it now logs at start), the front-camera low-light crash still
happened: the ArcSoft library is dlopened, and bionic resolves a
dlopened library's symbols from the namespace's global group (the
executable, LD_PRELOAD libraries and DF_1_GLOBAL libraries) and then
its own dependencies. A DT_NEEDED of the executable is in neither, so
the blob kept using libc's malloc and got no padding.

Link libcamhal_pad with -z global so the linker adds it to the global
group.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 camera/camhal_pad/Android.bp   | 4 ++++
 camera/camhal_pad/camhal_pad.c | 6 ++++--
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/camera/camhal_pad/Android.bp b/camera/camhal_pad/Android.bp
index ea18be4..ffe2598 100644
--- a/camera/camhal_pad/Android.bp
+++ b/camera/camhal_pad/Android.bp
@@ -6,6 +6,10 @@ cc_library_shared {
         "libdl",
         "liblog",
     ],
+    // DF_1_GLOBAL: the linker puts the library in every lookup's global group,
+    // so libraries the HAL dlopens (the ArcSoft one) also bind to this malloc.
+    // As a plain DT_NEEDED it only interposes for the executable's own tree.
+    ldflags: ["-Wl,-z,global"],
     cflags: [
         "-Wall",
         "-Werror",
diff --git a/camera/camhal_pad/camhal_pad.c b/camera/camhal_pad/camhal_pad.c
index de4062d..d76296e 100644
--- a/camera/camhal_pad/camhal_pad.c
+++ b/camera/camhal_pad/camhal_pad.c
@@ -10,8 +10,10 @@
  * allocations, free() and every other process are unaffected.
  *
  * It is linked in as the first DT_NEEDED of the camerahalserver blob
- * (extract-files.py), so its malloc family precedes libc's for the HAL and for
- * every library the HAL dlopens. LD_PRELOAD does not work here: init starts
+ * (extract-files.py) and built with -z global (DF_1_GLOBAL). The first makes
+ * its malloc family precede libc's for the HAL; the second puts it in the
+ * linker's global group, which is what lookups from dlopened libraries (the
+ * ArcSoft one) search first. LD_PRELOAD would do both, but does not work here: init starts
  * the HAL with an SELinux domain transition, the kernel then sets AT_SECURE,
  * and the linker ignores LD_PRELOAD under AT_SECURE. The policy exception that
  * would allow it (init noatsecure) is an AOSP neverallow.
